# Isaac Sim outputs — regenerated by ./start_sim_docker.sh on every run
out/

# logs/ is tracked on purpose: each run log is the evidence behind a number in the docs,
# and several conclusions here were overturned by re-reading one. 1.4 MB for 40 files.

# Isaac Sim caches (GB-scale, machine-specific)
.isaac-cache/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Telemetry runs ARE tracked, so a log can reach the analysis side through the repo
# instead of a side channel — their R2.1 asked for logs precisely because data/ was
# ignored on both branches. Keep this to short reference runs: their synthetic set alone
# is ~250 MB, and parquet in git history is permanent.
#
# The .npz is only the container-side intermediate on the way to parquet, so it is not
# tracked; tools/npz_to_parquet.py regenerates the parquet from it if ever needed.
data/*.npz

# bulk run bundles for hand-over (tools/package_handover.sh); never in git
handover/
.venv-pal/

# Analysis side (merged from the nithya branch): synthetic logs alone are ~250 MB, and data/real was their local
# copy of our old logs. Our own short reference runs in data/ stay tracked.
data/synthetic/
data/real/
.pytest_cache/
